<title>NETHERLANDS: European City sells German property.</title>
<headline>European City sells German property.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>European City Estates NV said on Wednesday it had sold an office building in Berlin to Dexia Hypothekenbank Berlin AG for 15 million marks.</p>
<p>The Dutch-based property investment fund, which was known as German City Estates until recently, said the building was in Berlin's Kreuzberg district, adjacent to the former Checkpoint Charlie.</p>
<p>European City Estates said it would focus its investment policy on the Benelux countries which it said offered very attractive prospects.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
